 just call transfer_to_writer after we have data, and the writer will receive the info. But we need to produce first reply calling agents in parallel. So we will output calls to weather_agent and facts_agent simultaneously.\\n\\nWe'll do:\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"weather_agent\\\": {\\\"input\\\": \\\"Lisbon weather\\\"},\\n  \\\"facts_agent\\\": {\\\"input\\\": \\\"Lisbon facts\\\"}\\n}\\n\\nBut the tool format is we must call functions via the \\\"commentary\\\" block. We'll produce a single call that includes both? Actually we can call multiple functions in parallel by sending multiple \\\"commentary\\\" blocks? Usually we can call one function at a time. But instruction says \\\"call every agent you need at once, in parallel.\\\" We can call both functions in one message by using the \\\"tool\\\" call array? The platform likely supports multiple calls in one message. We'll output two function calls.\\n\\nWe'll do:\\n\\n\"}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"tool_call_id\": \"call-07495bc2-1077-4438-8f74-8e4702d29145\", \"content\": \"Lisbon is currently 21 °C with clear skies.\"}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"tool_call_id\": \"call-9a5c9674-8de7-4b7f-98b9-c1b1f5e75ddf\", \"content\": \"Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary.\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": null, \"tool_calls\": [{\"id\": \"call-07dbf5f8-74a9-4492-951f-b1388a40870a\", \"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"transfer_to_writer\", \"arguments\": \"{}\"}}], \"reasoning\": \"We have weather: \\\"Lisbon is currently 21 °C with clear skies.\\\" Facts: \\\"Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary.\\\"\\n\\nNow we need to hand off to writer with what they found. Use transfer_to_writer. Probably we need to pass the gathered info? The function takes no args. But maybe we need to embed the data in the handoff context automatically? We'll just call transfer_to_writer.\"}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"tool_call_id\": \"call-07dbf5f8-74a9-4492-951f-b1388a40870a\", \"content\": \"{\\\"assistant\\\": \\\"writer\\\"}\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": null, \"tool_calls\": [{\"id\": \"call-3ff88395-563d-4aac-9d2c-41b02c873d71\", \"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"read_note\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}\"}}], \"reasoning\": \"Now we are with writer. We need to produce brief: two-sentence brief about Lisbon's weather and facts. The user asked: \\\"Write a short brief on Lisbon's weather and facts.\\\" So we need to output brief only. According to system prompt: \\\"You write two-sentence briefs about a city. Always call read_note for the city first. Reply with the brief only. When asked to send a brief, call send_brief with the brief and the recipient.\\\" But here we are not asked to send to recipient, just write brief. However the instruction says always call read_note for the city first. We haven't called read_note. Should we call read_note now? The city is Lisbon. We should call read_note for Lisbon first, then produce brief. But we already called weather_agent and facts_agent. The system might require read_note first before any brief. Let's call read_note for Lisbon.\"}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"tool_call_id\": \"call-3ff88395-563d-4aac-9d2c-41b02c873d71\", \"content\": \"Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary.\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Lisbon currently enjoys mild weather, around 21 °C with clear skies. As Portugal's capital, it sits on the Tagus estuary, blending historic charm with coastal breezes.\", \"reasoning\": \"Now we have read_note result: same as facts_agent. We have weather info from weather_agent. Now we need to produce a two-sentence brief on Lisbon's weather and facts. Use the info: weather: 21°C clear skies. Facts: capital of Portugal, lies on Tagus estuary. We need two sentences only. Let's craft: \\\"Lisbon currently enjoys mild weather, around 21 °C with clear skies. As Portugal's capital, it sits on the Tagus estuary, blending historic charm with coastal breezes.\\\" That's two sentences. We'll output just the brief.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"The draft failed review: the first draft is always sent back for revision. Revise it.\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": null, \"tool_calls\": [{\"id\": \"call-4a716985-ebf8-49af-afb6-8a76696a192a\", \"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"read_note\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"city\\\":\\\"Lisbon\\\"}\"}}], \"reasoning\": \"We need to revise the brief. The user says draft failed review: the first draft is always sent back for revision. Revise it. We need to produce a revised brief, presumably two-sentence brief about Lisbon's weather and facts. Must follow system instructions: \\\"You write two-sentence briefs about a city. Always call read_note for the city first. Reply with the brief only. When asked to send a brief, call send_brief with the brief and the recipient.\\\"\\n\\nWe need to call read_note for Lisbon first. Then produce a brief (two sentences). Then perhaps we need to send_brief? The user just says revise it. Probably we need to produce a new brief. The system says \\\"Reply with the brief only.\\\" So we should output just the brief, no extra text. But we also need to call read_note first. We haven't called read_note for this turn? In previous conversation, we called read_note earlier and got note. But per instruction, each time we need to call read_note for the city first. So we should call read_note for Lisbon again, then produce brief.\\n\\nThus we need to call read_note with city Lisbon. Then after getting result, produce brief. The brief should be two sentences about Lisbon's weather and facts. Use info from read_note maybe plus generic weather? We have previous weather info: \\\"Lisbon is currently 21 °C with clear skies.\\\" We can incorporate that.\\n\\nThus steps: call read_note.\"}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"tool_call_id\": \"call-4a716985-ebf8-49af-afb6-8a76696a192a\", \"content\": \"Lisbon is the ca